WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.005 --> 00:00:18.058
Since I had already cleaned my room, we decided to test the Amazing Mess-Pusher in Molly's room.

2
00:00:19.059 --> 00:00:22.242
We used it to push everything on the floor under Molly's bed.

3
00:00:22.262 --> 00:00:26.946
"Hey," said Molly, looking around her empty floor.

4
00:00:26.966 --> 00:00:29.548
"It really works, Iggy!"

5
00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:34.421
"Yeah, your room looks nice and neat," I said.

6
00:00:35.961 --> 00:00:39.302
That night I went to bed feeling happy about my new invention.

7
00:00:40.343 --> 00:00:42.703
I could help kids everywhere with their messy rooms!

8
00:00:43.764 --> 00:00:48.485
Maybe soon I'd also think of a new idea to help Molly with her monster problem.

9
00:00:51.706 --> 00:00:52.906
The next day Mrs.

10
00:00:52.966 --> 00:00:55.647
Romano asked us to take out our story ideas.

11
00:00:55.667 --> 00:01:00.332
"Tomorrow you will start writing your books," she said.

12
00:01:00.352 --> 00:01:03.794
"Make sure you have a really good plot idea."

13
00:01:03.814 --> 00:01:08.897
"Uh-oh," said Molly, rummaging through her backpack.

14
00:01:08.917 --> 00:01:12.979
"I think I left our list of plot ideas in my room."

15
00:01:14.921 --> 00:01:18.703
When we got home from school, Molly and I looked for our list in her room.

16
00:01:19.903 --> 00:01:21.624
But we couldn't find it.

17
00:01:21.644 --> 00:01:28.128
"I bet it got pushed under my bed with the Amazing Mess-Pusher," said Molly.

18
00:01:29.876 --> 00:01:31.397
Molly peered under her bed.

19
00:01:31.417 --> 00:01:33.379
"Oh no!"

20
00:01:33.959 --> 00:01:34.720
she cried.

21
00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:36.722
"What's the matter?"

22
00:01:37.162 --> 00:01:37.723
I asked.

23
00:01:37.743 --> 00:01:41.906
"There's nothing under my bed," said Molly.

24
00:01:41.926 --> 00:01:44.408
"Everything is gone!"

25
00:01:44.428 --> 00:01:48.571
"I wonder what happened," I said.

26
00:01:48.591 --> 00:01:53.976
"Maybe Caswell knows," said Molly.

27
00:01:56.724 --> 00:02:02.126
We went out to the living room, where Caswell and Lucy were watching another episode of Monster Madness.

28
00:02:06.487 --> 00:02:08.968
Molly said, trying not to look at the TV.

29
00:02:08.988 --> 00:02:12.009
"Did you take anything out of my room?"

30
00:02:12.029 --> 00:02:18.750
"Grr!" said Caswell, growling like the monster.

31
00:02:21.431 --> 00:02:23.652
But he shook his head to tell Molly "no."

32
00:02:25.236 --> 00:02:28.098
Lucy didn't know anything about the stuff under the bed either.

33
00:02:30.220 --> 00:02:33.603
We were still looking for our list when Molly's mom came home.

34
00:02:33.623 --> 00:02:38.627
"Mom, do you know what happened to the stuff under my bed?"

35
00:02:39.067 --> 00:02:39.828
asked Molly.

36
00:02:39.848 --> 00:02:44.472
"I cleaned the apartment this morning," said Mrs.

37
00:02:44.572 --> 00:02:47.854
O'Donnell. "I cleaned under your bed too."

38
00:02:47.874 --> 00:02:50.717
"Did you see a list?"

39
00:02:51.177 --> 00:02:51.958
Molly asked.

40
00:02:53.079 --> 00:02:54.420
Mrs. O'Donnell shrugged.

41
00:02:55.364 --> 00:02:59.067
"There was lots of stuff under your bed, Molly, including crumpled paper.

42
00:02:59.567 --> 00:03:00.768
I just threw everything out."

43
00:03:02.549 --> 00:03:05.231
So that was the end of our list of plot ideas.

44
00:03:06.332 --> 00:03:10.295
And that was the reason Molly and I had to start all over again.

45
00:03:12.076 --> 00:03:16.940
At school the next morning, everyone was complaining about how hard it was to think of plots for

46
00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:17.760
their stories.

47
00:03:18.941 --> 00:03:22.484
Mrs. Romano said Gina and Jake's story was missing a middle.

48
00:03:23.660 --> 00:03:27.123
"You only have a beginning and an end," Mrs.

49
00:03:27.183 --> 00:03:28.484
Romano explained.

50
00:03:28.504 --> 00:03:30.986
"How do you write a middle?"

51
00:03:31.567 --> 00:03:32.548
asked Jake.

52
00:03:32.568 --> 00:03:37.192
"Something has to go wrong," explained Mrs.

53
00:03:37.252 --> 00:03:41.515
Romano. "That gives a story suspense."

54
00:03:43.077 --> 00:03:46.480
Something definitely went wrong when I got home from school that day.

55
00:03:48.021 --> 00:03:51.424
There, in the middle of my room, was a garbage bag.

56
00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:54.621
On it was a note from Tate.

57
00:03:54.641 --> 00:03:59.164
"Dear Piggy, I found more junk in my closet.

58
00:04:00.165 --> 00:04:02.947
You can use your Amazing Mess-Pusher to clean it up.

59
00:04:03.807 --> 00:04:06.309
Just don't push any stuff under my bed!

60
00:04:06.649 --> 00:04:10.912
Tate." I'm normally a calm person.

61
00:04:11.613 --> 00:04:13.854
But at that moment I blew up.

62
00:04:14.595 --> 00:04:15.955
Everything was going wrong!

63
00:04:16.236 --> 00:04:19.818
My Amazing Mess-Pusher had caused our plot list to get thrown out.

64
00:04:20.499 --> 00:04:22.000
Molly was still not sleeping.

65
00:04:23.376 --> 00:04:26.758
And Tate was being mean and driving me crazy!

66
00:04:26.778 --> 00:04:29.499
"I can't stand it!"

67
00:04:29.899 --> 00:04:30.340
I yelled.

68
00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:32.521
"Nothing is going right!"

69
00:04:33.501 --> 00:04:36.903
Then I kicked the garbage bag as hard as I could.
